BT
/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 786 Tm (Laravel API Authentication and Rate Limiting) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 771 Tm () Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 756 Tm (1. Laravel Sanctum) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 741 Tm (Laravel Sanctum provides a lightweight authentication system for single page) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 726 Tm (applications, mobile applications and simple token based APIs. It offers two mechanisms:) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 711 Tm (API tokens and cookie based SPA authentication.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 681 Tm (API tokens are created with the createToken method on a user model that uses the) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 666 Tm (HasApiTokens trait. The plain text token is shown only once, at creation time. Sanctum) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 651 Tm (stores only a SHA-256 hash of the token in the personal_access_tokens table.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 621 Tm (Each token can carry abilities, which work like scopes. A route can require an ability) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 606 Tm (with the abilities or ability middleware, and the code can check) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 591 Tm ($user->tokenCan\('orders:read'\) before acting.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 576 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 561 Tm (Tokens do not expire by default. Set the expiration option in config/sanctum.php \(a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 546 Tm (number of minutes\) to make them expire, and run the sanctum:prune-expired Artisan) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 531 Tm (command on a schedule to delete expired rows.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 516 Tm () Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 501 Tm (2. Protecting routes) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 486 Tm (Attach the auth:sanctum middleware to any route or route group that needs an) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 471 Tm (authenticated user. Requests must send the token in the Authorization header as a Bearer) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 456 Tm (token. A request without a valid token receives a 401 Unauthorized response.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 441 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 426 Tm (To revoke access, delete the token with) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 411 Tm ($request->user\(\)->currentAccessToken\(\)->delete\(\), or delete all of a user's tokens with) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 396 Tm ($user->tokens\(\)->delete\(\).) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 381 Tm () Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 366 Tm (3. Rate limiting) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 351 Tm (Laravel includes a rate limiter built on the cache. Named limiters are defined in the) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 336 Tm (boot method of AppServiceProvider \(or RouteServiceProvider in older versions\) with) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 321 Tm (RateLimiter::for\(\). A limiter returns a Limit object, for example) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 306 Tm (Limit::perMinute\(60\)->by\($request->user\(\)?->id ?: $request->ip\(\)\).) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 291 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 276 Tm (Apply a limiter to a route with the throttle middleware, for example throttle:api. When) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 261 Tm (the limit is exceeded Laravel returns a 429 Too Many Requests response and includes a) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 246 Tm (Retry-After header.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 231 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 216 Tm (The default api limiter allows 60 requests per minute per user or IP address. Login) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 201 Tm (endpoints deserve a stricter limiter, such as five attempts per minute, to slow down) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 186 Tm (password guessing.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 171 Tm () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 156 Tm (The rate limiter stores its counters in the default cache store. With several) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 141 Tm (application servers use a shared store such as Redis, otherwise each server counts) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 126 Tm (separately and the real limit is higher than configured.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 111 Tm () Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 96 Tm (4. Practical checklist) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 81 Tm (Always send API traffic over HTTPS. Give tokens the smallest abilities they need. Expire) Tj
ET
